`# AI BUILDING SAAS — PROJECT MEMORY & PHASE TRACKER
# File: .memory
# Last Updated: 2026-09-17
# Based on: Phased Product Requirements Document (PRD)

================================================================================
EXECUTIVE SUMMARY & PRODUCT VISION
================================================================================
Core Mission:
Real plan generation, complete site utilization (100% plot accounting), and
conceptual structural coordination with columns and beams.

Non-Negotiable Product Principles:
1. Canonical Building Model remains the sole source of truth for site, floors,
   rooms, walls, openings, structural concepts, and audit metadata. 2D SVG,
   Three.js 3D scenes, and UI components are projections of this model.
2. The 100% Site-Utilization Invariant:
   Plot area = Setbacks / Protected Reserve
             + Building Footprint
             + Parking (with road-connected maneuvering)
             + Landscape / Garden
             + Circulation (Pedestrian + Vehicle)
             + Services
             + Future Expansion / Declared Open Space
   *No residual site area may be displayed as unexplained blank space.*
   *Full plot classification is mandatory; full building coverage is not.*
   *The 50x50 plot issue: The generator sizes the footprint to the requested
   program rather than stretching rooms. The bug is leaving residual land
   unassigned, not failing to stretch the building.*
3. Safety & Professional Boundaries:
   Columns and beams are conceptual planning aids only. They must be explicitly
   labeled "Conceptual / Engineer Review Required" until approved by a licensed
   structural engineer. No code compliance or member adequacy may be claimed.
4. Truthful AI & Generation Provenance:
   Studio generation runs locally and deterministically; external LLMs are
   optional and backend-dependent. The UI and candidate records must truthfully
   report provenance (direct user brief, rule-based parser, local fallback, or
   provider LLM), never implying AI generation when running locally.

================================================================================
CANONICAL MODEL SPECIFICATION (TARGET STATE)
================================================================================
Entities to exist in `@ai-floor-planner/core`:
- SiteZone:
    id: string
    kind: 'setback' | 'parking' | 'garden' | 'pedestrian_circulation' |
          'vehicle_circulation' | 'service' | 'future_expansion'
    boundary: Polygon
    area: number
    accessLinks: readonly string[]
    source: 'RULE_BASED' | 'USER_DEFINED' | 'GENERATED'
    reviewStatus: 'UNREVIEWED' | 'REVIEWED' | 'LOCKED'
- StructuralGrid:
    id: string
    floorScope: readonly number[]
    gridlinesX: readonly { id: string; x: number; label: string; locked: boolean }[]
    gridlinesY: readonly { id: string; y: number; label: string; locked: boolean }[]
    spacing: { min: number; max: number; target: number }
    provenance: string
    lockState: boolean
    reviewStatus: 'CONCEPTUAL' | 'REVIEWED'
- Column:
    id: string
    position: Point
    footprint: Polygon | { width: number; depth: number }
    supportedLevels: readonly number[]
    gridReference?: string
    conceptualDimensions: { widthMm: number; depthMm: number; shape: 'rectangular' | 'circular' }
    status: 'CONCEPTUAL' | 'LOCKED' | 'ENGINEER_REVIEW_REQUIRED'
- Beam:
    id: string
    floorLevel: number
    startSupport: { entityId: string; type: 'column' | 'wall' }
    endSupport: { entityId: string; type: 'column' | 'wall' }
    sectionPlaceholders: { widthMm: number; depthMm: number }
    spanMm: number
    status: 'CONCEPTUAL' | 'UNSUPPORTED' | 'EXCESSIVE_SPAN' | 'VALID'
- GenerationAudit:
    seed: number
    requirementsHash: string
    engineVersions: { core: string; planning: string; geometry: string }
    providerProvenance: 'DIRECT_BRIEF' | 'RULE_BASED' | 'PROVIDER_LLM' | 'LOCAL_FALLBACK'
    providerModel?: string
    diagnostics: readonly DiagnosticIssue[]
    siteUtilizationBalance: {
      plotAreaMm2: number
      allocatedAreaMm2: number
      unallocatedAreaMm2: number
      categories: Record<string, number>
    }
    approvalState: 'UNREVIEWED' | 'REVIEWED' | 'EXPORTED'

